  "email": "ryan.brooks@brightline.example",
  "reason": "KB-005 quick check: confirm status of the former employee account with reported failed logins (read-only, for security escalation)"
}

{
  "user_id": 10,
  "reason": "KB-005 quick check: review reported failed sign-in attempts on disabled former-employee account for security escalation"
}

{
  "summary": "P1 security. Reported by: Priya Nair (IT Manager, priya.nair@brightline.example), who saw failed-login alerts on the account of former employee Ryan Brooks (user_id 10, Sales AE, left spring 2026). Findings: account status = disabled (offboarded), BUT sign_in_blocked = false and vpn_access = TRUE. That looks like an offboarding gap. Password last set 2026-03-23. Sign-in logs (14d): 2 failed_password attempts against VPN on 2026-10-09 at 07:05 and 07:07 UTC (03:05/03:07 ET, overnight at home) from IP 192.0.2.140, a hosting network in Amsterdam, NL, with no MFA. This fits someone trying stolen or old credentials. No successful sign-ins seen. Actions taken: none. Per KB-005, Tier 1 did not reset, unlock, or block, and the account belongs to someone other than the ticket sender. Still needed: security review of the attempts and IP; decide whether to block sign-in and remove the leftover VPN access; check whether the Brooks credentials appear elsewhere (reuse or breach); check the VPN gateway for other attempts from 192.0.2.140; then follow up with Priya.",
  "reason": "KB-005 says always escalate; P1 security; possible credential stuffing on a disabled account that still has VPN access"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Priya, thanks for flagging this. Ryan Brooks' account is disabled, and nobody has signed in successfully. There were two failed attempts to sign in to the VPN with his account early Friday morning (around 3 AM Eastern) from a hosting provider in Amsterdam. We also found that VPN access was never removed from his account when he left. Because this could be someone trying stolen or old credentials, I've sent it to our Tier 2 security team as urgent. They'll review the attempts, decide on next steps like blocking sign-in and removing the leftover VPN access, and follow up with you.",
  "internal_note": "Sender: Priya Nair (IT Manager, uid 3). Subject account: Ryan Brooks (uid 10, former employee): status disabled, but sign_in_blocked=false and vpn_access=true (likely offboarding gap). Logs: 2 failed_password attempts on VPN, 2026-10-09 07:05 and 07:07 UTC (03:05 ET), from IP 192.0.2.140, a hosting network in Amsterdam, NL, no MFA. No successful sign-ins. Following KB-005, I did not reset, unlock, or block. The account isn't the sender's, so block_sign_in was left for Tier 2/security to decide. Escalated to Tier 2 as P1 (escalation id 1).",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-005"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
